## 16. Key Takeaways
1. **Physics must ground the AI**: Pure data-driven models fail catastrophically on Out-of-Distribution (OOD) data. The TrustSense-BMS virtual sensor must incorporate thermal ODEs (like Joule heating and cooling) either in the loss function (PINN) or as a baseline predictor.
2. **Parallel > Series for Spatiotemporal Data**: When analyzing battery metrics, processing spatial features (which cell) and temporal features (recent history) in parallel yields better stability than stacking them in series.
3. **Uncertainty is Mandatory**: A single point prediction is dangerous. Using methods like GPR or Quantile Regression to output confidence bounds is critical for the "Safety Supervisor" module to trigger fallbacks.

